EXTENSION "ARMDef_Guardians_of_the_Forests_TribunalHistory_FeliciaFollowerOfBonisagus" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Guardians of the Forests - Felicia, follower of Bonisagus"
    VERSION "0.5.1"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_Guardians_of_the_Forests_Core_Ext"

    # Felicia, follower of Bonisagus (Chapter Three: Tribunal History & Customs, p23): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #t61e13b1dd2e9cdd9881f2f ^"Felicia, follower of Bonisagus" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Characteristics" STRING "Int +2, Per 0, Pre 0, Com 0, Str 0, Sta +1, Dex +2, Qik 0"
            ^"Size" STRING "0"
            ^"Age" STRING "24 (24) (Journeyman)"
            ^"Decrepitude" STRING "0"
            ^"Warping Score" STRING "0 (0)"
            ^"Confidence Score" STRING "1 (3)"
            ^"Virtues and Flaws" STRING "The Gift; Journeyman; Major Magical Focus (weather); Cyclic Magic (Positive) — Winter months, Free Study, Linden Gild Trained, Personal Vis Source, Puissant Intrigue, Skilled Parens; Favors (to Fengheld), Study Requirement; Busybody, Cyclic Magic (Negative) — Summer months"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Loner +2, Self-Reliant +1, Suspicious –2"
            ^"Reputations" STRING "None"
            ^"Combat" STRING "Dodging: Init 0, Attack n/a, Defense 0, Damage n/a"
            ^"Soak" STRING "+1"
            ^"Fatigue Levels" STRING "OK, 0, –1, –3, –5, Unconscious"
            ^"Wound Penalties" STRING "–1 (1-5), –3 (6-10), –5 (11-15), Incapacitated (16-20)"
            ^"Abilities" STRING "Artes Liberales 2 (Latin script), Athletics 1 (sprinting), Awareness 1 (ambushes), Bargain 2 (food), Bavaria Lore 1 (woods), Chirurgy 1 (sprains), Civil and Canon Law 1 (vagabond laws), Concentration 2 (Auram), Disguise 2 (as a man), Dominion Lore 1 (roadside shrines), Faerie Lore 1 (weather spirits), Finesse 1 (Auram), Folk Ken 3 (travelers), Harz Mountains Lore 2 (sites to study), High German 5 (disguising accent), Hunt 1 (small game), Intrigue 2+2 (Hermetic), Latin 4 (Hermetic usage), Magic Theory 4 (weather spells), Music 1 (flute), Order of Hermes Lore 2 (covenants), Parma Magica 2 (Corpus), Penetration 1 (Auram), Rhine Lore 1 (towns), Saxony Lore 1 (safe roads), Survival 2 (summer), Swim 1 (rivers)"
            ^"Arts" STRING "Cr 9, In 2, Mu 2, Pe 2, Re 7; An 1, Aq 7, Au 9, Co 1, He 0, Ig 0, Im 0, Me 0, Te 0, Vi 2"
            ^"Twilight Scars" STRING "None"
            ^"Equipment" STRING "Good quality clothes."
            ^"Encumbrance" STRING "0 (0)"
            ^"Spells Known" STRING "Ward Against Faeries of the Water (ReAq 15) +15 Chaos of the Angry Wave (ReAq 20) +15 Jupiter’s Resounding Blow (CrAu 10) +28 Stench of the Twenty Corpses (CrAu 10) +19 Broom of the Winds (CrAu 15) +28 Clouds of Rain and Thunder (CrAu 25) +28 Ward Against Rain (ReAu 10) +24 Ward Against Faeries of the Air (ReAu 15) +17 Clouds of Thunderous Might (ReAu 30) +24"
            ^"Appearance" STRING "Felicia is a sturdily-built woman, whose weather-beaten features are easily mistaken for those of a young man, which allows her to travel alone without complications. Her straggly blond hair is usually mostly hidden under a hat, although wisps invariably escape its confines."
            ^"Source" STRING "Guardians of the Forests"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 23
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Felicia is the filia of Dorana of Fengheld, the most prominent member of the lineage of Irmele, and a Hermetic descendent of Trianoma. As expected, Felicia has taken directly to the open road to familiarize herself with the Tribunal’s covenants. Her magic waxes and wanes with the seasons; during the winter she will find a covenant in which to overwinter, when her magic is strongest. During summer, when her magic is weakest, she will take to the road, seeking out natural phenomena which are necessary for her study. Fengheld has promised that she can use a spare laboratory in the winter if they have one, in return for favors as yet unspecified. Felecia is freshly Gauntleted and may be suitable for a player character, although she will only loosely associate herself with a covenant, due to her frequent travel.\n\nStory Seed: A Peace Emissary\n\nFelecia arrives at the player covenant to stay over winter, with the aim of negotiating peace between them and an enemy covenant of the magi. Since she visited the enemy covenant first — indeed she may well have just arrived from there the previous spring — the magi might suspect an ulterior motive, although she has none."
    }

}
